cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GIB-15K, please cite it as below."
title: "GIB-15K: The Illusion of Grounding — A Diagnostic Benchmark for Multimodal RAG under Retrieval Noise, Visual Ambiguity, and Cross-Modal Conflict"
abstract: >-
  GIB-15K is a diagnostic benchmark of 15,000 image-QA pairs, drawn from COCO
  and Visual Genome and labelled by hallucination sub-type (object / attribute /
  relation). Each pair carries three adversarial variants applied at controlled
  dosages: retrieval noise (hard negatives), visual ambiguity (blur / motion /
  low-resource cropping), and cross-modal conflict (with counterfactual twins).
  The benchmark combines dosage-response curves, an internal attention audit, and
  a human ceiling in a single instrument, and includes a machine-computable
  failure taxonomy (Knowledge Inertia / Sensory Capture / Reasoning Collapse).
type: dataset
